messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: python/libxml.c
Line: 552
Function: libxml_xmlOutputBufferClose
Bug type: use-after-free
CWE: CWE-416
Explanation: xmlOutputBufferClose(out) frees the underlying xmlOutputBufferPtr, but the Python wrapper object is not updated to clear its internal pointer. Subsequent API calls using the same Python object (e.g., xmlOutputBufferFlush) will retrieve and use a freed pointer, leading to a use-after-free.

Source context:
```c
      512:     obj = PyoutputBuffer_Get(buffer);
      513:     if (obj == NULL) {
      514: 	fprintf(stderr,
      515: 	        "outputBufferGetPythonFile: obj == NULL\n");
      516: 	Py_INCREF(Py_None);
      517: 	return(Py_None);
      518:     }
      519: XML_IGNORE_DEPRECATION_WARNINGS
      520:     if (obj->closecallback != xmlPythonFileClose) {
      521: 	fprintf(stderr,
      522: 	        "outputBufferGetPythonFile: not a python file wrapper\n");
      523: 	Py_INCREF(Py_None);
      524: 	return(Py_None);
      525:     }
      526:     file = (PyObject *) obj->context;
      527:     if (file == NULL) {
      528: 	Py_INCREF(Py_None);
      529: 	return(Py_None);
      530:     }
      531: XML_POP_WARNINGS
      532:     Py_INCREF(file);
      533:     return(file);
      534: }
